# SOVEREIGN INTELLIGENCE REPORT - task_00516988

## Summary
Knowledge Base Grounded Answer: Lockout/Tagout (LOTO) is an essential industrial safety procedure (NOVA-SOP-2024-08) designed to prevent unexpected machine startup or hazardous energy release during maintenance.

HOW LOTO WORKS STEP-BY-STEP:
1. Preparation: Identify all electrical, mechanical, and hydraulic power sources.
2. Machine Shutdown: Deactivate equipment using normal operational controls.
3. Energy Isolation: Open main high-voltage circuit breakers to disconnect power.
4. Lockout/Tagout Application: Place physical padlocks (Lockout) and warning tags (Tagout) on all energy isolating devices.
5. Stored Energy Dissipation: Bleed residual hydraulic pressure and discharge electrical capacitors.
6. Zero-Energy Verification: Test start controls to confirm 100% zero energy before maintenance.

Mandate: Immediate LOTO isolation is mandatory if pump operating temperature exceeds 85.0°C or vibration exceeds 4.5 mm/s RMS.

